# Regression fixture for inc-32tj: a permanent field must survive a day change.
#
# Depth 2, because Player::Rest refuses on depth 1 by design ("you can just
# climb back out of the dungeon entirely"). Genocide first, because the rest is
# refused while any hostile is in plain sight. The subject is a torch archon:
# wizard placement leaves it non-SUMMONED, an archon is NOT hostile to this
# character so it never blocks the rest, and its light/aura field is permanent
# (Dur -1). Resting with lowercase 'z' is the only route that both advances
# theGame->Day -- so Map::DaysPassed runs -- and leaves the player on the same
# map, which the surface inn does not: the inn's Descend regenerates the level.
#
# 'z' must be lowercase. KY_CMD_SLEEP is { 'Z', 0 } and the keyset compares
# modifier flags exactly, so a shifted 'Z' matches nothing (src/KeyScript.cpp:22).

@include chargen.keys
@until "HP:" ESC

w y
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "torch archon"
RIGHT ENTER

w
@choose "Display Resource Statistics"
DOWN*30
@dump:fields-before
ESC

z y
SPACE SPACE

w
@choose "Display Resource Statistics"
DOWN*30
@dump:fields-after
ESC
@quit
